In the seventeenth century it would be natural to ask: how would a free 
society solve the problems of women dying while giving birth or infant
mortality (and high mortality of children)? Someone, hypothetically, could
ask that. And conclude that government should put all resources in research
in those areas. But at that time  n o b o d y  could know how the problem
would be solved.
I am not a libertarian, I am an Objectivist. I want a government, a very small
one, and able to enforce the law. If the government runs education of citizens
who then vote for represenatives who write laws which the government enforces,
there is a clear and obvious conflict of interest. So our children in public
schools are educated that the greatest human beings are politicians, not
scientists (and I am biased towards scientists, as you see). They are educated
that people need to be controlled and told what to do, and that government
has to protect the people from greedy big business. 
Any economic function performed by the government becomes a tool in controlling
citizens. Plus the economic function does not get done. 
How would the homeless problem be solved in the free society? As if the
controlled society solved it!
Betsy says that if we went straight to a libertarian "no government" society
there would be warlords and gangs who would take over. We will not go straight 
to an anarcho-Capitalist society. I believe we will either evolve into a 
society with minimal use of force (i.e., minimal government) or we will
become extinct. Evolve, gradually. So the point is to seek the next evolution
step. In the United States I believe the next step will have to involve
privatization of education and decriminalization of drugs.
In other words -- say you want to eliminate the income tax. You may want to 
start by campaigning for raising the 0% tax bracket and for full inflation
indexing of brackets and other parts of the code every year.
Or, if you want to campaign for privatization of Social Security, 
introduce a 0% payroll tax bracket. If the people working for minimum wage
have such a hard time, and the greedy Capitalists pay them so little, how
come the government can claim such an outrageous percentage of their
wages. Those people are better off not working and going on Medicaid when
they are old.

I firmly believe that people are motivated either by greed or power lust.
I like greed.

